            "review_title": "Review at Musa Curry India",
            "review_text": "danmaio\nPerth, Australia88 contributions\n0\nGreat tasting curry\nOct 2017 • Couples\nI have been here numerous times since 2010, an absolutely love it. Full of locals and hidden away down a laneway near the Windsor Plaza Hotel. I am amazed at the mixed reviews here. It's goat curry, definitely goat. The taste of the curry is divine, and soaking the banh mi in the curry and eating that is just beautiful. Look, if you looking for Indian, steer clear, it's not Indian. If you looking for 4 or 5 star dinning, don't bother going. If goat skin in your meal and bones bother you, then you won't enjoy it. If taste and flavour and lots of it is what you want , in a laid back place, not expensive, then you will love it. \nPs. You just have to look at the bones to know it's not beef.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 17, 2017",
