            "review_title": "Review at Musa Curry India",
            "review_text": "John T\nLos Angeles, California13 contributions\n0\nA bit pricey, not as good as previously before\nApr 2017 • Friends\nDefinitely a local spot. I've eaten at Musa Curry on a number of occasions previously before on my trips to Vietnam, however, this time around it wasn't as enjoyable as before.\n\nThe cost for a plate of curry goat is 160k VND, which isn't bad, but you don't really get that much goat, so I felt the food did not merit the price. \n\nI also found a few strands of black hair on my food. I was told by the waitress that the hair belonged to the goat, which did not make me feel too much better, so I asked for a new plate which they promptly brought over.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 16, 2017",
